WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.680
Good afternoon. Thank you very much.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:19.100
Today I am present to inform you that the Western world is facing a significant threat.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:25.500
It is in danger because those who are supposed to defend the values of the Western world

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.660
are co-opted by a worldview that inevitably leads to socialism

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.780
and consequently to poverty and economic deprivation.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.640
Unfortunately, in recent decades,

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.800
motivated by some well-intentioned desires to help others

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.820
and others by the desire to belong to a privileged caste,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.740
the main leaders of the Western world have abandoned the model of freedom

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.240
for different versions of what we call collectivism.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:07.200
We are here to tell you that collectivist experiments are never the solution to the problems that afflict the citizens of the world, but rather they are their cause.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:14.360
Trust me, there is no one better than us Argentines to provide testimony on these two issues.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:22.600
When we embraced freedom in 1860, in 35 years we became the world's first dominant power.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.640
35 years we became the first world power

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.280
while when we embraced collectivism

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.380
over the past 100 years

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.380
we saw how our citizens began to systematically

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.060
impoverish themselves

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.500
until they fell to the 140th position in the world

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.040
40 in the world

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.580
but before we can have this discussion

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.380
it would be important for us to first look

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.840
at the data that supports why free market capitalism

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.060
is not only a possible system

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.560
to end world poverty

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.460
but also the only morally desirable system to achieve it.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:02.040
If we consider the history of economic progress,

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.420
we can see how from year zero until around 1800,

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.380
the world's per capita GDP remained practically constant throughout the reference period.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.120
If one looks at a chart of the evolution of economic growth throughout human history,

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.800
one would be seeing a chart with the shape of a hockey stick

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:26.680
an exponential function that remained constant for 90% of the time

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.220
and exponentially shoots up from the 19th century.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:37.940
The sole exception to this stagnant history was at the end of the 15th century with America's discovery.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:47.080
Except for this, from year 0 to 1800, global per capita GDP remained stagnant without any significant changes.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:54.920
Now, not only did capitalism generate an explosion of wealth from the moment it was adopted as an economic system,

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:02.580
but if one analyzes the data, what is observed is that growth has been accelerating throughout the entire period.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:13.720
During the entire period between years 0 and 1800, the per capita GDP growth rate remains stable at around 0.02% annually,

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.500
that is, practically without growth.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:23.560
From 19th century with industrial revolution, growth rate reaches 0.66%.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:31.120
Given the current rate, it would require a time span of approximately 107 years to achieve a two-fold increase in per capita GDP.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.280
In 1900-1950, growth rate rises to 1.66% annually.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.320
150, growth rate rises to 1.36% annually.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:47.960
We no longer need 107 years to double per capita GDP, but 66.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:56.300
If we take the period between 1950 and the year 2000, we can see that the growth rate was 2.1% annually,

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:01.840
which would mean that in just 33 years, we could double the world's per capita GDP.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.300
This trend, far from stopping, remains alive even now.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:19.580
If we consider the period from 2000 to 2023, the growth rate increased again at 3% per year, meaning we could double our per capita GDP globally in only 23 years.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:28.260
Now, when studying per capita GDP from 1800 to today, what is observed is that after the

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:34.720
Industrial Revolution, global per capita GDP multiplied by more than 15 times, generating

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.720
an explosion of wealth that lifted 90% of the world's population out of poverty.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:47.500
We must never forget that by the year 1800, about 95% of the world's population lived

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:54.200
in extreme poverty, while that number dropped to 5% by the year 2020 prior to the pandemic.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:02.420
The conclusion is obvious. Far from being the cause of our problems, free market capitalism

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:09.280
as an economic system is the only tool we have to end hunger, poverty, and destitution throughout

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:16.840
the planet. The empirical evidence is unquestionable. Therefore, as there is no doubt that free market

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:22.960
capitalism is superior in productive terms, the left's doxa has attacked capitalism for

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:30.840
its moral issues, for being, according to them, as its detractors say, unjust.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:36.460
They claim capitalism is bad because it's individualistic and collectivism is good because

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.500
it's altruistic towards others.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.240
And thus they strive for social justice.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:48.040
this concept that has become trendy in the developed world recently, in my country, it has

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:55.240
been a constant in political discourse for over 80 years. The issue is that social justice is unfair

00:05:55.240 --> 00:06:02.180
and doesn't contribute to general well-being. On the contrary, it's an inherently unfair idea

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:08.260
because it's violent. It's unfair because the state is financed through taxes and taxes are

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:14.200
collected coercively, or can any of us confidently say that they pay taxes of their own free will?

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.940
This implies that the state is funded through coercion and that the higher the tax burden,

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:27.200
the greater the coercion, leading to a reduction in freedom. Those who promote social justice start

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:32.480
from the idea that the economy as a whole is a cake that can be distributed in a different way.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:41.020
But that cake is not given. It is wealth that is generated in what, for example, Israel Kirshner calls a market discovery process.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:50.280
If the good or service that a company offers is not desired, that company goes bankrupt unless it adapts to what the market is demanding.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:07:02.520
Create a high-quality product at a good price or attractive, succeed and produce more, so the market is a process of discovery where the capitalist finds the right direction on the go.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:17.660
But if the state punishes the capitalist for success and blocks him in this process, it destroys his incentives, and the consequences are that he will produce less and the cake will be smaller, generating harm to society.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:31.760
Collectivism, by inhibiting discovery and hindering appropriation, ties the entrepreneur's hands, preventing him from producing better goods and offering better services at a better price.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:50.780
How can it be then that from academia, international orgs, politics and econ theory, an econ system is demonized that not only has lifted 90% of the world's pop out of extreme poverty and does so increasingly faster, but is also fair and morally superior?

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:56.180
Thanks to capitalism, the world is currently in its best moment.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:01.900
There has never been a moment in history with greater prosperity than the one we live in today.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:08.420
Today's world is freer, richer, more peaceful, and more prosperous than ever before.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:14.400
This is true for everyone, but particularly for those countries that are free,

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:18.300
where they respect economic freedom and individual property rights.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:22.920
because free countries are 12 times richer than repressed ones.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.740
Saying goes that in countries with freedom,

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:30.140
people live better than 90% of population in repressed countries.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:34.000
It has 25 times fewer poor people in the standard format

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.260
and 50 times fewer in the extreme format.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.160
And if that weren't enough,

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.300
citizens of free countries live 25% longer

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.360
than citizens of repressed countries.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.100
Now, in order to understand what we come to defend,

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:52.820
it is important to define what we mean when we talk about libertarianism.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:09:01.000
To define it, I take up the words of the greatest proponent of the ideas of freedom in Argentina,

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:03.760
Professor Alberto Venegas Lynch,

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:09.980
who says that libertarianism is the unrestricted respect for the life project of others,

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:12.660
based on the principle of non-aggression,

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:17.140
and in defense of the right to life, liberty, and property,

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:23.400
whose fundamental institutions are private property, free markets without state intervention,

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:30.320
free competition, division of labor, and social cooperation, where one can only be successful

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:37.860
by serving others with goods of better quality at a better price. In other words, the capitalist,

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:45.520
the successful entrepreneur, is a social benefactor who contributes to the well-being of society as a

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:54.020
whole. In short, a successful entrepreneur is a hero. This is the model that we are proposing for

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:59.920
the future of Argentina, a model based on the fundamental principles of libertarianism,

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:08.540
the defense of life, freedom, and property. Now, if free market capitalism and economic freedom

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:14.360
have been remarkable instruments to eradicate poverty globally, and we are presently experiencing

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:20.640
the most favorable period in human history, it is worth inquiring why I assert that the West is in

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:29.000
jeopardy. I argue that the West is endangered as in countries defending free market, private property,

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:35.000
and other institutions of libertarianism, sectors of the political and economic establishment,

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:41.840
due to errors in their theoretical framework and ambition for power, undermine libertarianism,

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:48.860
opening doors to socialism and potentially condemning us to poverty misery and stagnation

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:55.220
because it should never be observed that socialism is always and everywhere impoverishing

00:10:55.220 --> 00:11:02.360
failed in all countries were attempted it was a failure economically it was a failure socially

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:07.700
it was a failure culturally and it also killed more than a hundred million human beings

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:33.120
The main problem of the West today is that we not only have to confront those who, even after the fall of the wall and overwhelming evidence, continue to advocate for impoverishing socialism, but also our own leaders, thinkers, and academics who, sheltered in a misguided framework, undermine the foundations of the system that has given us the greatest wealth and prosperity in our history.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:40.600
The theoretical framework I am referring to is neoclassical economic theory, which designs

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:46.260
an instrument unintentionally functional to the intrusion of the state, socialism, and

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.720
the degradation of society.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:54.420
The issue with neoclassicals is that since the model they fell in love with doesn't match

00:11:54.420 --> 00:12:00.740
reality, they attribute the error to the supposed market failure instead of revising the premises

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:01.480
of their model.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:17.300
On the text about a supposed market failure, regulations are introduced that only generate distortions in the price system that hinder economic calculation and consequently savings, investment and growth.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:24.100
This problem essentially lies in the fact that not even supposedly libertarian economists

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:29.220
understand what the market is, since if it were understood, it would quickly be seen

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:33.160
that it is impossible for there to be such a thing as a market failure.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:40.400
The market is not just a graphical description of a supply curve and a demand curve on a graph.

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:46.880
The market is a mechanism of social cooperation where property rights are voluntarily exchanged.

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:53.680
Thus, considering this definition, discussing market failure is a contradiction in terms.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.920
There is no market failure.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:03.480
If transactions are voluntary, the only situation in which there can be a market failure is

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:08.400
if there is coercion present, and the only one with the ability to coerce in a generalized

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:12.340
manner is the state that possesses the monopoly of violence.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:21.400
Consequently, if someone considers that there is a market failure, I would recommend that they check if there is state intervention in the middle

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:27.460
If no state intervention found, suggest reanalyzing as it is definitely wrong

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:31.420
Market failures do not exist

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:39.240
An example of the alleged market failures described by neoclassicals are concentrated structures in the economy

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:55.780
However, without functions that demonstrate increasing returns to scale, whose counterpart are the concentrated structures of the economy, we would be unable to explain the phenomenon of economic growth from 1800 to the present day.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:58.140
Look how interesting.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:10.440
Commencing from the year 1800 and extending onwards, with the population experiencing a multiplication of more than eight or nine times,

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:16.280
the per capita income underwent a growth of more than 15 times in magnitude.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:22.980
To clarify, there are more returns. This caused poverty to drop from 95% to 5%.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:29.440
However, the presence of increasing yields implies the existence of concentrated structures,

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:35.160
which would be referred to as, for example, a monopoly in the market economy.

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:42.700
How can it be that something that has generated so much well-being, according to neoclassical

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:45.360
theory, that is considered a market failure?

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:51.100
Neoclassical economists think outside the box.

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.840
When the model fails, don't get angry with reality.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.700
Get angry with the model and change it.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:04.360
The dilemma for the neoclassical model is that they aim to enhance market functioning

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.420
by targeting perceived failures.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:12.540
By doing so, they not only open doors to socialism, but also undermine economic growth.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:19.360
For instance, implementing regulations on monopolies, dismantling their profits,

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:24.740
and obliterating increasing returns would inevitably annihilate economic growth.

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:30.800
In other words, each time you want to correct a presumed market failure,

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:37.200
inevitably, due to not knowing the market or because you have become attached to a failed model,

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:41.660
you are opening doors to socialism and condemning people to poverty.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:49.100
However, in the face of the theoretical demonstration that state intervention is harmful,

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:53.120
the empirical evidence that it failed because it could not be otherwise,

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:59.340
the solution that collectivists will propose is not greater freedom, but greater regulation,

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:04.460
generating a downward spiral of regulations until we all become poorer

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:08.880
and the lives of all of us depend on a bureaucrat sitting in a luxury office.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:16.420
Given the resounding failure of collectivist models and the undeniable advances of the free world,

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.000
socialists were forced to change their agenda.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:30.680
They left behind the class struggle based on the economic system to replace it with other supposed social conflicts equally harmful to community life and economic growth.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:37.160
The first of these new battles was the ridiculous and unnatural fight between man and woman.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:42.660
Libertarianism already establishes equality between sexes.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:46.800
The cornerstone of our creed states that all men are created equal,

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:50.820
that we all have the same unalienable rights granted by the Creator,

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:54.240
among which are life, liberty, and property.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:17:00.080
This radical feminism agenda has led to increased state intervention,

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.260
hindering the economic process.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:07.560
It provides jobs to bureaucrats who haven't contributed anything to society,

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:13.040
whether through women's ministries or international organizations promoting this agenda.

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:19.260
Another conflict that socialists pose is that of humans against nature.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:25.320
They argue that humans cause harm to the planet and that it must be protected at all costs,

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:32.680
even advocating for population control mechanisms or supporting the controversial agenda of abortion rights.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:39.780
Unfortunately, these harmful ideas have strongly permeated our society.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:45.340
Neo-Marxists have managed to co-opt the common sense of the Western world.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:54.080
They achieved this through the appropriation of the media, culture, universities, and yes, even international organizations.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:18:05.320
The final case is very serious, as it involves institutions with huge influence on the political and economic decisions of the countries in these multilateral organizations.

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:25.800
Fortunately, more of us dare to raise our voices as we see that if we don't confront these ideas head-on, the only possible destiny is more state, more regulation, more socialism, more poverty, less freedom, and consequently, a worse quality of life.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:31.560
Unfortunately, the West has already started down this path.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:37.440
To many, it may sound ridiculous to suggest that the West has embraced socialism,

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:45.140
but this view is only ridiculous if one limits themselves to the traditional economic definition of socialism,

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:50.220
which states that it is an economic system where the state owns the means of production.

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:58.460
In my opinion, this definition needs to be updated to reflect the current circumstances from my perspective.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:06.080
Today, states don't need to control means of production to control every aspect of individuals' lives.

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:18.400
With tools such as monetary issuance, debt, subsidies, interest rate control, price controls, and regulations to correct alleged market failures,

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:22.260
they can control the destinies of millions of human beings.

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:27.980
This is how we have reached the point where, with different names or forms,

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:34.820
good parts of the politically accepted offers in most Western countries are generally collectivist variants.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:43.880
Whether they openly declare themselves as communists, fascists, Nazis, socialists, social democrats,

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:50.660
national socialists, Christian Democrats, Keynesians, Neo-Keynesians, progressives,

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:57.780
populists, nationalists, or globalists. In the end, there are no substantive differences.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:02.500
Everyone argues that the state should control all aspects of individuals' lives.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:09.240
All define a model contrary to the one that led humanity to the most spectacular progress in its

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:15.560
history. We are here today to extend an invitation to the other Western countries to resume the

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:21.560
path towards prosperity. Economic freedom, limited government, and unrestricted respect

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:28.900
for private property are vital for economic growth. The impoverishment that collectivism

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:35.660
produces is not a fantasy, nor is it fatalism. It is a reality that Argentinians have known

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:42.200
very well for at least 100 years. Because we have already experienced it, we have already gone

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:47.540
through this. Because as I said before, since we decided to abandon the model of freedom that had

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:52.680
made us rich, we are trapped in a downward spiral where we are getting poorer every day.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:21:01.800
This is, we have already experienced it ourselves, and we are here to warn you about what can happen

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:08.040
if Western countries who became rich with the model of freedom continue on this path of servitude.

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:14.960
The Argentine case is the empirical proof that regardless of wealth, natural resources,

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:22.020
population capability, education level, or the amount of gold bars in the central bank's coffers,

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:28.860
these factors do not guarantee success. If measures are adopted that hinder the free

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:34.860
functioning of markets, free competition, free price systems, if trade is hindered,

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:39.860
if private property is attacked, the only possible destination is poverty.

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:48.340
To summarize, I want to convey a message to all entrepreneurs present and those who are not,

00:21:48.860 --> 00:21:53.380
but are following us from around the globe, whether they're here or not, physically.

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:59.820
Don't be intimidated by the political caste or the parasites who live off the state

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:06.120
Don't yield to a political class that only wants to prolong its power and preserve its privileges

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:08.840
You are social benefactors

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.280
You are heroes

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:15.700
You are the creators of the most extraordinary era of prosperity we have ever experienced

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:19.620
Don't let anyone say ambition is immoral

00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:26.680
If you earn money, it's because you provide a superior product, better price, contributing to well-being

00:22:26.680 --> 00:22:29.860
Do not yield to the advance of the state

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:33.900
The state is not the solution, the state is the problem itself

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:37.320
You are the true protagonists of this story

00:22:37.320 --> 00:22:42.200
And know that from today, you have Argentina as an unconditional ally

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:45.760
Thank you very much and long life freedom, Dammit

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:54.820
Thanks, thanks.
